        "timestamp": 1778821708
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I just opened PR <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39435\">#39435</a> and it passed the CI checks. I decided to only start with <code>Int.closure_eq_zmultiples</code> for now in the spirit of doing things in small chunks. Please let me know if I need to do change anything, and I plan to work on the other suggested theorems in the mean time!</p>",
        "id": 595407379,
        "sender_full_name": "Tadd Yuchi Mao",
        "timestamp": 1778883402
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>One potentially interesting project is Burnside’s theorem on solvability of groups of order p^a q^b. It might take a while, though.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I heard this was formalised by an LLM as part of lean-eval. Please don't quote me</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Indeed this was formalized as early as May 8 with Aleph Prover, and there have been 7 solutions so far:<br>\n<a href=\"https://lean-lang.org/eval/problems/finite_group_isSolvable_of_card_eq_prime_pow_mul_prime_pow/\">https://lean-lang.org/eval/problems/finite_group_isSolvable_of_card_eq_prime_pow_mul_prime_pow/</a></p>",
